course: dictionary
lesson: 11344
title: Many meanings of zero
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Zero is a small word with many jobs. In maths it means none at all, and it is also the starting point on a ruler. When you meet zero in a text, read the words around it to find which meaning the writer wants. «It's giving zero interest,» Bertie mutters. The words around zero tell you it means none at all, and «it's giving» means it looks like.
explain: Zero can also be a point on a scale. The clue is in the object: a ruler, a thermometer or a number line. On a thermometer, zero degrees Celsius is the temperature where water freezes. Ask yourself what would fit in the place of the word. If you can swap in "none" or "the starting point" and the sentence still makes sense, you have found the meaning.
explain: Zero can also be a verb in a phrase. To zero in on something means to aim straight at it or focus on it closely. The meaning changes with the words that come with it, so always read the whole phrase, not just the single word.
fact: Zero is the number 0, which means none or nothing at all.
fact: Zero is the point on a scale where counting starts, such as 0 on a ruler.
fact: Zero degrees Celsius is the temperature at which water freezes.
fact: «Zero in on» means to aim straight at something or focus on it closely.
fact: In a number like 2,030, the zero is a place holder that keeps the other digits in the right places.
exercise: «It's giving zero interest,» Bertie mutters. What does zero interest mean here? | Interest in zero degrees | A small, friendly interest | A very high amount of interest | *None at all
exercise: On a ruler, where does counting start? | One hundred | Half | *Zero | Ten
exercise: «An overdraft lets you spend below zero, which is borrowing.» What does spending below zero mean? | *Spending money you do not have, by borrowing it | Spending zero pounds on food | Spending less money than you have in the bank | Spending money on a cold day
test: At what temperature in Celsius does water freeze? | Five degrees | Ten degrees | Fifty degrees | *Zero degrees
test: To zero in on something means to | Run away from it quickly | Forget all about it | *Aim straight at it or focus on it closely | Count backwards from ten
exam: In the number 2,030, what job does the zero do? | Shows that the number is negative | Shows the number is very small | *Holds a place so the other digits stay in the right places | Means that nothing is important
